    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 1000 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near Lynch, or 14 miles southeast of Spencer, moving east at 45 mph. HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Locations impacted include... Lynch, Bristow, Monowi, Dorsey, Scottville, and Redbird State Wildlife Management Area. This includes the following highways... Highway 281 near mile marker 205. Highway 12 between mile markers 130 and 144.",
